  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Accident Report Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an accident report form?\", \"a\": \"An accident report form is the written record of an accident at work or on the road. It records the time and place and who was involved. A factual account of what happened follows, with any injuries or damage. Insurers and HR teams use it to open claims.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create an accident report form?\", \"a\": \"Decide which accidents get reported, what each report has to capture, and who receives each type. Put all of it in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. The result is a form people can file from a phone, with every report landing in a table you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of an accident report form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Picture a delivery driver rear-ended at a stop sign. The form opens with the date, the time, and the intersection. The driver's name and van number sit below. The other car's plate and insurer go beside the police report number. Photos of both bumpers and a witness's phone number come last, before a few sentences on what happened, in order.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an auto accident report form include?\", \"a\": \"Record each driver's license and insurer, along with the plates and the crash location. Add the police report number, photos of the damage, and witness contacts. A commercial vehicle accident report form also asks for the unit number and the load. Pair it with a vehicle inspection form to log the truck's condition before its next run.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between an injury report form and an accident report form?\", \"a\": \"Scope. An injury report form records one person who got hurt, down to the body part and the treatment. An accident report form covers more ground, including crashes and property damage where nobody was injured. One form can handle both, with injury questions that appear only when someone was hurt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a free accident report form template?\", \"a\": \"Check with your insurer or employer first, and use their version if they have one. Universities and government agencies also post free copies, and form builders offer an accident report form template to start from. Emergent builds the same fields from a plain-English description, with no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I customize an accident report form template?\", \"a\": \"Cut every question that does not fit the accidents you handle. A vehicle accident report form needs plates and a police report number, while injury questions ask what hurts and who treated it. Show each section only when it applies. Then rename fields in the words reporters use and choose who gets each kind of report.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which fields belong on an injury report form?\", \"a\": \"Start with who was hurt and the task under way when it happened. Add the date and place, then the body part and any first aid or clinic visit. Close with witness names and the supervisor who filed it. A motor vehicle accident report form keeps these questions and adds plates and insurers on top.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an injury report form be used for near misses?\", \"a\": \"Not usually. An injury report form is built around a person who got hurt, and a near miss leaves no injury to record. Log near misses on an incident report form instead, with the hazard and the person who will fix it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you fill out an auto accident report form online?\", \"a\": \"Yes, and a phone at the scene is the best place to do it, while plates and witness names are easy to get. Photos go straight into the report instead of sitting in a camera roll. A car accident report form built with Emergent keeps every report in a database you own.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}